{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>And his garments</b> — four times in the Masorah: <b>ובגדיו קרועים</b> (and his garments were torn); <b>ובגדיו לא יפרום</b> (and his garments he shall not tear); <b>ובגדיו</b> (and his garments), <b>לא תשרפנה</b> (you shall not burn them). Even though a mourner is obligated in tearing, as it is written <b>ובגדיו קרועים</b> — for he mourned over the killing of Saul the anointed priest — he (the high priest) does not tear, as it is written <b>ובגדיו לא יפרום</b> (and his garments he shall not tear), for he is holy, and his garments are holy. And therefore <b>ובגדיו לא תשרפנה</b> — that the priestly garments were not burned when Nadav and Avihu were burned, according to the one who says their bodies were burned and their garments remained intact."], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {0 "The word ד׳ at the opening means 'four' — i.e., four occurrences of ובגדיו in the Masorah, the three cited plus the lemma word from the current verse. The phrase 'שאול כהן גדול' refers to King Saul, called 'the anointed priest' in rabbinic tradition (he was anointed like a priest)."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:14:44.830757017Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}